==Low German==
''Mecklenburgic-Western Pomeranian dialects''

===Alternative forms===

* {{l|nds|he}} (can also be found in Mecklenburgic-Western Pomeranian dialects)

===Etymology===

From {{etyl|osx|nds}} {{term|hē||he|lang=osx}} from {{proto|Germanic|hiz|his, this one|lang=nds}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|k'e-||k'ey-|this, here|lang=nds}}. Cognate with {{en}} {{term|he||he|lang=en}}, {{nl}} {{term|hij||he|lang=nl}}, {{da}} {{term|han||he|lang=da}}. Related to {{l|en|here}}.

===Pronunciation===

* {{IPA|/hɛɪ̯/|/haɪ̯/|lang=nds}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|nds|pronoun|g=m|genitive|sin|dative|em|dative 2|jüm|accusative|en}}

# {{personal|lang=nds}} [[he]]

====Usage notes====
* Which dative is employed depends on dialect, not on function.
* Some dialects might consider any of the inflected forms obsolete.

